  "title": "Trump Says Iran Wants a Deal but Its Terms Fall Short",
  "deck": "Iran’s foreign minister says Tehran still sees a diplomatic path and wants guarantees against renewed fighting. Qatar says mediation continues.",
  "category": "world",
  "categoryLabel": "World News",
  "type": "article",
  "author": "EP News",
  "publishedAt": "2026-11-21T00:52:55.976Z",
  "updatedAt": "2026-11-21T00:52:55.976Z",
  "body": [
    "President Donald Trump said Friday that Iran wants an agreement to end hostilities with the United States, but that Tehran is unwilling to accept terms he considers sufficient. Iranian Foreign Minister Abbas Araqchi said Tehran still sees a way to end the war through diplomacy and wants guarantees against another round of fighting.",
    "Speaking at the White House on Nov. 20, Trump repeated that the United States would prevent Iran from acquiring a nuclear weapon. His public remarks did not lay out the full terms Washington would accept.",
    "Araqchi told Iran’s state-owned Iran newspaper that Tehran wants assurances that Washington is serious about negotiations. He said Iran considers keeping its enriched uranium inside the country a red line, while leaving room for what he described as a fair solution.",
    "Qatar’s Foreign Ministry said Tuesday that it was still working to narrow the gap between Washington and Tehran. Reuters reported that Qatari and Iranian officials met that day as part of the mediation effort.",
    "The latest statements leave two questions for mediators: what limits on Iran’s nuclear program Washington would accept, and what guarantees Tehran would consider sufficient to prevent renewed fighting. Neither government announced an agreement Friday."
  ],
